        "explanation": "<h3>Mastering the 4 Operations</h3><p>Maths is built on four pillars: Addition (+), Subtraction (-), Multiplication (×), and Division (÷).</p><h4>Integer Rules</h4><ul><li><strong>Adding Negatives:</strong> 5 + (-3) is the same as 5 - 3 = 2.</li><li><strong>Subtracting Negatives:</strong> 5 - (-3) becomes 5 + 3 = 8. (Minus minus is plus!)</li><li><strong>Multiplying/Dividing:</strong><ul><li>Same signs = Positive result (e.g., -2 × -3 = 6)</li><li>Different signs = Negative result (e.g., -2 × 3 = -6)</li></ul></li></ul><h4>BODMAS</h4><p>Order matters! <strong>B</strong>rackets first, then <strong>O</strong>rders (powers), <strong>D</strong>ivision/<strong>M</strong>ultiplication, finally <strong>A</strong>ddition/<strong>S</strong>ubtraction.</p>",
